Dialogue: 3,0:05:07.29,0:05:13.04,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}A PATROL MOVES FORWARD · LORRAINE
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.93,0:05:18.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And the dirt of northern France had been farmed and
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.89,0:05:21.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}fertilized with manure for centuries.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.05,0:05:23.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}It was full of bacteria that live without oxygen.
Dialogue: 2,0:05:16.18,0:05:21.93,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 802 0 l 802 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:05:16.18,0:05:21.93,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:05:16.18,0:05:21.93,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:05:16.18,0:05:21.93,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}THE RUINS OF ESNES · MEUSE-ARGONNE
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.10,0:05:45.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}It spread fast.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.02,0:05:48.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}That is why the Army's surgeons talked about 12 hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.32,0:05:51.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}If a wound could be cleaned out surgically within
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.31,0:05:54.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}about 12 hours, the man's chances were far better.
Dialogue: 2,0:05:44.35,0:05:50.10,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 789 0 l 789 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:05:44.35,0:05:50.10,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:05:44.35,0:05:50.10,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:05:44.35,0:05:50.10,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}SUPPLY COLUMNS · MEUSE-ARGONNE
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.57,0:06:15.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The battalion surgeon taught every man how to put it on.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.01,0:06:17.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The idea was simple:
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.24,0:06:20.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}cover the wound and protect it from more damage,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.19,0:06:21.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}until help arrived.
Dialogue: 2,0:06:12.82,0:06:18.57,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 789 0 l 789 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:06:12.82,0:06:18.57,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:06:12.82,0:06:18.57,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:06:12.82,0:06:18.57,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}42ND DIVISION TRENCHES · LORRAINE
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.62,0:06:32.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Their job was to find the wounded, mark where they
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.44,0:06:33.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}lay, and gather them.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.62,0:06:36.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}About four in ten of the wounded could still walk,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.45,0:06:38.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}and they made their own way back.
Dialogue: 2,0:06:29.87,0:06:35.62,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 789 0 l 789 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:06:29.87,0:06:35.62,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:06:29.87,0:06:35.62,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:06:29.87,0:06:35.62,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}A PATROL MOVES FORWARD · LORRAINE
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.76,0:06:40.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Everyone else had to be carried.
Dialogue: 2,0:06:39.01,0:06:40.72,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 995 0 l 995 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:06:39.01,0:06:40.72,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:06:39.01,0:06:40.72,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:06:39.01,0:06:40.72,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}WOUNDED CARRIED TO THE REAR · MEUSE-ARGONNE
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.38,0:06:51.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The mud was sometimes up to their knees.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.50,0:06:53.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The wooden handles of the stretchers rotted and
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.98,0:06:56.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}splintered, and the bearers' hands were covered in
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.62,0:06:57.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}blisters and splinters.
Dialogue: 2,0:06:49.63,0:06:55.38,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 789 0 l 789 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:06:49.63,0:06:55.38,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:06:49.63,0:06:55.38,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:06:49.63,0:06:55.38,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}STRETCHER BEARERS · 42ND DIVISION
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.28,0:07:01.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}They drew their own maps of the trenches, and redrew
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.19,0:07:03.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}them as the trenches collapsed under shellfire.
Dialogue: 2,0:06:58.53,0:07:04.22,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 789 0 l 789 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:06:58.53,0:07:04.22,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:06:58.53,0:07:04.22,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:06:58.53,0:07:04.22,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}42ND DIVISION TRENCHES · LORRAINE
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.27,0:07:07.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}They were not armed, and they were not protected.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.10,0:07:09.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Their only shield was the Red Cross on their
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.64,0:07:12.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}armband, and in an artillery war, a shell does not
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.53,0:07:13.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}read armbands.
Dialogue: 2,0:07:04.52,0:07:10.27,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 995 0 l 995 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:07:04.52,0:07:10.27,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:07:04.52,0:07:10.27,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:07:04.52,0:07:10.27,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}AID STATION · 89TH DIVISION · MEUSE-ARGONNE
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.79,0:07:17.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And the hardest part of the job, as one history of
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.04,0:07:18.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}them puts it, was this:
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.54,0:07:21.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}to carry a man through enemy fire, and find, when
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.73,0:07:24.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}they finally reached the aid station, that he was
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.92,0:07:25.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}already dead.
Dialogue: 2,0:07:14.04,0:07:19.79,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 789 0 l 789 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:07:14.04,0:07:19.79,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:07:14.04,0:07:19.79,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:07:14.04,0:07:19.79,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}42ND DIVISION TRENCHES · LORRAINE
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.21,0:07:29.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Under fire, the carry back often had to wait for night.
Dialogue: 2,0:07:26.46,0:07:29.51,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 789 0 l 789 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:07:26.46,0:07:29.51,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:07:26.46,0:07:29.51,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:07:26.46,0:07:29.51,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}THE MEUSE VALLEY · NOV. 1918
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.24,0:07:39.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Then the bearers came, and you were carried to the
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.07,0:07:40.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}first real stop on the chain:
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.71,0:07:42.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}the battalion aid station.
Dialogue: 2,0:07:36.49,0:07:42.24,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 802 0 l 802 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:07:36.49,0:07:42.24,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:07:36.49,0:07:42.24,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:07:36.49,0:07:42.24,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}AID STATION DUGOUT · 42ND DIVISION
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.64,0:07:46.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}It sat about 500 to 1,000 yards behind the line, in
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.19,0:07:49.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}a dugout, or in whatever building still stood.
Dialogue: 2,0:07:42.89,0:07:48.64,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1231 0 l 1231 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:07:42.89,0:07:48.64,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:07:42.89,0:07:48.64,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}U.S. ARMY PHOTO · MEDICAL DEPT. HISTORY, VOL. VIII (1925)
Dialogue: 3,0:07:42.89,0:07:48.64,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}DRESSING STATION AT BETRICAMP, FRANCE · APRIL 20, 1918
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.83,0:08:00.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Here the doctor did what he could, and only that.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.78,0:08:02.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Iodine around the wound.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.23,0:08:03.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}A fresh dressing.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.26,0:08:05.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Something to stop the bleeding.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.13,0:08:06.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Morphine for the pain.
Dialogue: 2,0:07:58.08,0:08:03.83,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1510 0 l 1510 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:07:58.08,0:08:03.83,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:07:58.08,0:08:03.83,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}U.S. ARMY PHOTO · MEDICAL DEPT. HISTORY, VOL. VIII (1925)
Dialogue: 3,0:07:58.08,0:08:03.83,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}REGIMENTAL AID STATION, 28TH INFANTRY, NEAR CANTIGNY · MAY 28, 1918
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.91,0:08:09.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Blankets, and a hot drink, because the doctors had
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.81,0:08:12.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}learned that a wounded man who was cold and wet was
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.77,0:08:14.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}more likely to go into shock.
Dialogue: 2,0:08:07.16,0:08:12.91,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 802 0 l 802 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:08:07.16,0:08:12.91,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:08:07.16,0:08:12.91,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:08:07.16,0:08:12.91,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}AID STATION DUGOUT · 42ND DIVISION
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.91,0:08:17.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And a shot of tetanus antitoxin.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.11,0:08:18.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Every wounded man got one.
Dialogue: 2,0:08:15.16,0:08:19.30,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 867 0 l 867 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:08:15.16,0:08:19.30,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:08:15.16,0:08:19.30,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:08:15.16,0:08:19.30,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}AID STATION · ANSAUVILLE · ST. MIHIEL
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.46,0:08:35.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Once every wounded man got the shot, the rate fell
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.70,0:08:38.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}to about 1.5 per 1,000 within three months.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.48,0:08:41.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}At American aid stations, the shot was routine.
Dialogue: 2,0:08:32.71,0:08:38.46,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 995 0 l 995 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:08:32.71,0:08:38.46,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:08:32.71,0:08:38.46,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:08:32.71,0:08:38.46,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}AID STATION · 89TH DIVISION · MEUSE-ARGONNE
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.97,0:08:44.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Then the doctor filled out a field medical card for you.
Dialogue: 2,0:08:42.22,0:08:45.36,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1017 0 l 1017 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:08:42.22,0:08:45.36,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:08:42.22,0:08:45.36,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:08:42.22,0:08:45.36,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}WALKING WOUNDED WITH TAGS · ST. NAZAIRE AREA
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.70,0:08:52.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}But if the shell had broken your thigh bone, there
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.45,0:08:54.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}was one more thing the aid station could do.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.87,0:08:57.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And it was the difference between life and death.
Dialogue: 2,0:08:49.95,0:08:55.70,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 995 0 l 995 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:08:49.95,0:08:55.70,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:08:49.95,0:08:55.70,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:08:49.95,0:08:55.70,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}AMBULANCES NEAR BERTRICHAMP · 42ND DIVISION
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.70,0:09:03.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Early in the war, a soldier whose thigh bone was
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.79,0:09:06.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}shattered by a shell or a bullet, a so-called open
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.00,0:09:09.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}femur fracture, was very likely to die.
Dialogue: 2,0:09:00.95,0:09:06.70,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 995 0 l 995 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:09:00.95,0:09:06.70,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:09:00.95,0:09:06.70,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:09:00.95,0:09:06.70,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}WOUNDED CARRIED TO THE REAR · MEUSE-ARGONNE
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.42,0:09:19.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The femur, the thigh bone, is the longest bone in
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.05,0:09:19.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}the body.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.54,0:09:21.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Shattered, it is very hard to hold still.
Dialogue: 2,0:09:16.67,0:09:22.15,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1296 0 l 1296 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:09:16.67,0:09:22.15,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:09:16.67,0:09:22.15,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}U.S. ARMY MANUAL OF SPLINTS AND APPLIANCES · 1917
Dialogue: 3,0:09:16.67,0:09:22.15,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}THOMAS TRACTION LEG SPLINT, APPLIED IN BED · LINE DRAWING
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.20,0:09:24.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And without support, every jolt of a stretcher,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.89,0:09:27.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}across shell holes and duckboards, moved the broken
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.81,0:09:28.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}bone again.
Dialogue: 2,0:09:22.45,0:09:28.20,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 789 0 l 789 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:09:22.45,0:09:28.20,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:09:22.45,0:09:28.20,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:09:22.45,0:09:28.20,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}STRETCHER BEARERS · 42ND DIVISION
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.89,0:09:30.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The answer was an old invention.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.97,0:09:34.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}A frame of iron with a padded ring at the top and a
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.27,0:09:37.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}bar at the bottom, designed in Liverpool in the
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.31,0:09:41.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}1870s by a surgeon and bone-setter named Hugh Owen Thomas.
Dialogue: 2,0:09:29.14,0:09:34.89,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 953 0 l 953 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:09:29.14,0:09:34.89,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:09:29.14,0:09:34.89,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}U.S. ARMY MANUAL OF SPLINTS AND APPLIANCES · 1917
Dialogue: 3,0:09:29.14,0:09:34.89,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}THOMAS TRACTION LEG SPLINT · LINE DRAWING
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.86,0:10:09.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}One British surgical history describes bearers
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.69,0:10:12.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}crawling out into no-man's-land at night to splint a
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.88,0:10:14.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}wounded man's leg where he lay.
Dialogue: 2,0:10:07.11,0:10:12.86,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1360 0 l 1360 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:10:07.11,0:10:12.86,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:10:07.11,0:10:12.86,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}U.S. ARMY MANUAL OF SPLINTS AND APPLIANCES · 1917
Dialogue: 3,0:10:07.11,0:10:12.86,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}THOMAS SPLINT APPLIED FOR STRETCHER TRANSPORT · LINE DRAWING
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.64,0:10:27.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}From four in five, to about one in six.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.00,0:10:30.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Historians warn that faster ambulances and better
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.96,0:10:32.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}hospitals helped too.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.23,0:10:35.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}But the splint is still credited with much of that change.
Dialogue: 2,0:10:25.89,0:10:31.64,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1231 0 l 1231 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:10:25.89,0:10:31.64,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:10:25.89,0:10:31.64,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1917–18 · RED CROSS / SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:10:25.89,0:10:31.64,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}LOADING A STRETCHER · AMERICAN DRIVERS WITH THE FRENCH
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.18,0:10:39.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}When the Americans came, the Thomas splint was part
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.10,0:10:42.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}of the standard kit at their battalion aid stations.
Dialogue: 2,0:10:36.43,0:10:42.18,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 995 0 l 995 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:10:36.43,0:10:42.18,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:10:36.43,0:10:42.18,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:10:36.43,0:10:42.18,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}AMBULANCES NEAR BERTRICHAMP · 42ND DIVISION
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.54,0:10:45.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}A piece of iron from the 1870s turned out to be one
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.85,0:10:48.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}of the great lifesavers of the war.
Dialogue: 2,0:10:42.79,0:10:48.53,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1167 0 l 1167 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:10:42.79,0:10:48.53,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:10:42.79,0:10:48.53,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}U.S. ARMY MANUAL OF SPLINTS AND APPLIANCES · 1917
Dialogue: 3,0:10:42.79,0:10:48.53,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}TRACTION BED FRAME FOR LEG FRACTURES · LINE DRAWING
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.58,0:10:50.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Now you had to get to a surgeon.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.42,0:10:53.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And between you and him were some of the most jammed
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.43,0:10:54.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}roads of the war.
Dialogue: 2,0:10:48.83,0:10:54.58,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 845 0 l 845 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:10:48.83,0:10:54.58,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:10:48.83,0:10:54.58,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:10:48.83,0:10:54.58,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}TRAFFIC ON THE ROADS · MEUSE-ARGONNE
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.50,0:11:00.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}From the aid station, the bearers carried you back
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.85,0:11:03.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}to where the ambulances could reach.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.26,0:11:06.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Behind every American division was a unit called the
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.74,0:11:08.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}sanitary train, about 950 men.
Dialogue: 2,0:10:57.75,0:11:03.50,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 888 0 l 888 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:10:57.75,0:11:03.50,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:10:57.75,0:11:03.50,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:10:57.75,0:11:03.50,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}RED CROSS AMBULANCES · CHATEAU-THIERRY
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.09,0:11:21.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The horse company was usually held back.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.42,0:11:24.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Horses were slow, they tired quickly, and they made
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.40,0:11:25.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}a large target.
Dialogue: 2,0:11:19.34,0:11:25.09,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 789 0 l 789 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:11:19.34,0:11:25.09,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:11:19.34,0:11:25.09,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:11:19.34,0:11:25.09,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}42ND DIVISION · LORRAINE SECTOR
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.73,0:11:28.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Often, the ambulance that came for you was a Ford.
Dialogue: 2,0:11:25.98,0:11:28.82,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1017 0 l 1017 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:11:25.98,0:11:28.82,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:11:25.98,0:11:28.82,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}U.S. ARMY PHOTO · MEDICAL DEPT. HISTORY, VOL. VIII (1925)
Dialogue: 3,0:11:25.98,0:11:28.82,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}SECTION NO. 646, U.S. ARMY AMBULANCE SERVICE
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.92,0:11:40.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}It was light enough that when it got stuck in a
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.36,0:11:43.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}hole, a few soldiers could simply lift it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.72,0:11:47.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}By November 1, 1918, 4,362 of them had been shipped
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.45,0:11:48.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}overseas.
Dialogue: 2,0:11:37.17,0:11:42.92,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1188 0 l 1188 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:11:37.17,0:11:42.92,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:11:37.17,0:11:42.92,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1917–18 · RED CROSS / SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:11:37.17,0:11:42.92,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}AMERICAN VOLUNTEER AMBULANCE DRIVERS WITH THE FRENCH
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.56,0:11:51.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The other common Army ambulance was the heavier White.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.80,0:11:54.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}It carried four stretcher patients, a driver and a
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.80,0:11:57.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}medic, at about twenty miles an hour.
Dialogue: 2,0:11:48.81,0:11:54.56,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1746 0 l 1746 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:11:48.81,0:11:54.56,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:11:48.81,0:11:54.56,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}U.S. ARMY PHOTO · MEDICAL DEPT. HISTORY, VOL. VIII (1925)
Dialogue: 3,0:11:48.81,0:11:54.56,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}AMBULANCE COMPANIES NO. 317 AND 318, 80TH DIVISION, VAUX, ARDENNES · NOV. 1918
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.48,0:12:00.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}This film shows American volunteer drivers serving
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.49,0:12:03.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}with the French Army, carrying French wounded.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.26,0:12:06.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Their ambulances and their roads looked much the same.
Dialogue: 2,0:11:57.73,0:12:03.48,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1188 0 l 1188 132 l 0 132{\p0}
