Dialogue: 3,0:27:45.45,0:27:51.20,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:27:45.45,0:27:51.20,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}A U.S. ARMY HOSPITAL WARD · ST. NAZAIRE AREA
Dialogue: 0,0:28:03.26,0:28:05.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Some wounds stayed deadly no matter what.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:05.91,0:28:09.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In British hospitals, even with surgery, more than
Dialogue: 0,0:28:09.15,0:28:12.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}half of the men with penetrating wounds of the
Dialogue: 0,0:28:12.13,0:28:12.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}abdomen died.
Dialogue: 2,0:28:03.51,0:28:09.26,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 789 0 l 789 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:28:03.51,0:28:09.26,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:28:03.51,0:28:09.26,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:28:03.51,0:28:09.26,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}TENT CAMP · MEUSE-ARGONNE
Dialogue: 0,0:28:28.84,0:28:31.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Not every wound, though, could be seen on an X-ray.
Dialogue: 2,0:28:29.09,0:28:31.76,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 789 0 l 789 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:28:29.09,0:28:31.76,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:28:29.09,0:28:31.76,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:28:29.09,0:28:31.76,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}42ND DIVISION TRENCHES · LORRAINE
Dialogue: 0,0:28:34.79,0:28:36.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Soldiers called it shell shock.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:36.79,0:28:39.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Men who had no visible injury, but who shook, or
Dialogue: 0,0:28:39.89,0:28:42.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}could not speak, or could not stop reliving what
Dialogue: 0,0:28:42.98,0:28:43.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}they had seen.
Dialogue: 2,0:28:35.04,0:28:40.79,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 789 0 l 789 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:28:35.04,0:28:40.79,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:28:35.04,0:28:40.79,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:28:35.04,0:28:40.79,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}42ND DIVISION TRENCHES · LORRAINE
Dialogue: 0,0:28:49.86,0:28:52.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The man who shaped the American response was a
Dialogue: 0,0:28:52.87,0:28:55.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}psychiatrist named Thomas Salmon.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:55.03,0:28:58.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In May 1917 he went to Britain to study how the
Dialogue: 0,0:28:58.10,0:28:59.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}British handled it.
Dialogue: 2,0:28:50.11,0:28:55.86,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 789 0 l 789 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:28:50.11,0:28:55.86,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:28:50.11,0:28:55.86,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:28:50.11,0:28:55.86,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}42ND DIVISION TRENCHES · LORRAINE
Dialogue: 0,0:28:59.79,0:29:03.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}At home, Army screening had already rejected about
Dialogue: 0,0:29:03.23,0:29:05.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}2% of recruits on mental grounds.
Dialogue: 2,0:29:00.04,0:29:05.79,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 789 0 l 789 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:29:00.04,0:29:05.79,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:29:00.04,0:29:05.79,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:29:00.04,0:29:05.79,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}42ND DIVISION TRENCHES · LORRAINE
Dialogue: 0,0:29:10.84,0:29:12.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Each division got a psychiatrist.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:12.81,0:29:15.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}A man brought in shaking was given rest, food and
Dialogue: 0,0:29:15.73,0:29:18.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}sleep, near his own unit, with the expectation that
Dialogue: 0,0:29:18.77,0:29:19.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}he would go back.
Dialogue: 2,0:29:11.09,0:29:16.84,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 931 0 l 931 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:29:11.09,0:29:16.84,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:29:11.09,0:29:16.84,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:29:11.09,0:29:16.84,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}A LETTER READ TO A PATIENT · AISNE-MARNE
Dialogue: 0,0:30:07.52,0:30:09.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Modern historians are more careful.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:09.82,0:30:13.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}A 2007 study of one British forward unit found that
Dialogue: 0,0:30:13.16,0:30:16.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}fewer than one in five of its men went straight back
Dialogue: 0,0:30:16.57,0:30:19.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}to combat, and called the wartime statistics
Dialogue: 0,0:30:19.45,0:30:21.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}inaccurate and misleading.
Dialogue: 2,0:30:07.77,0:30:13.52,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 931 0 l 931 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:30:07.77,0:30:13.52,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:30:07.77,0:30:13.52,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:30:07.77,0:30:13.52,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}A LETTER READ TO A PATIENT · AISNE-MARNE
Dialogue: 0,0:30:44.18,0:30:47.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Some of the men who came home carried this wound for
Dialogue: 0,0:30:47.21,0:30:48.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}years after the guns stopped.
Dialogue: 2,0:30:44.43,0:30:49.30,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 789 0 l 789 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:30:44.43,0:30:49.30,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:30:44.43,0:30:49.30,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:30:44.43,0:30:49.30,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}THE MEUSE VALLEY · NOV. 1918
Dialogue: 0,0:30:49.35,0:30:52.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}There was another, humbler wound of the trenches:
Dialogue: 0,0:30:52.17,0:30:52.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}the feet.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:52.69,0:30:55.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Trench foot came from days of cold, wet feet in
Dialogue: 0,0:30:55.39,0:30:56.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}leaking boots.
Dialogue: 2,0:30:49.60,0:30:55.35,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 789 0 l 789 132 l 0 132{\p0}
