Dialogue: 3,0:30:49.60,0:30:55.35,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:30:49.60,0:30:55.35,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}42ND DIVISION TRENCHES · LORRAINE
Dialogue: 0,0:31:14.48,0:31:17.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And while the armies fought, a different enemy was
Dialogue: 0,0:31:17.22,0:31:18.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}already inside the camps.
Dialogue: 2,0:31:14.73,0:31:18.99,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 789 0 l 789 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:31:14.73,0:31:18.99,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:31:14.73,0:31:18.99,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:31:14.73,0:31:18.99,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}TENT CAMP · MEUSE-ARGONNE
Dialogue: 0,0:31:21.79,0:31:24.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In the autumn of 1918, at the same time as the
Dialogue: 0,0:31:24.77,0:31:28.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Meuse-Argonne, the deadliest flu pandemic in modern
Dialogue: 0,0:31:28.08,0:31:30.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}history swept through the Army.
Dialogue: 2,0:31:22.04,0:31:27.79,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 802 0 l 802 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:31:22.04,0:31:27.79,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:31:22.04,0:31:27.79,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:31:22.04,0:31:27.79,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}AMERICAN RED CROSS OUTPOST SERVICE
Dialogue: 0,0:31:58.40,0:32:00.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The flu filled more beds than the enemy did.
Dialogue: 2,0:31:58.65,0:32:01.20,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1017 0 l 1017 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:31:58.65,0:32:01.20,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:31:58.65,0:32:01.20,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:31:58.65,0:32:01.20,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}A U.S. ARMY HOSPITAL WARD · ST. NAZAIRE AREA
Dialogue: 0,0:32:01.25,0:32:04.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}During the Meuse-Argonne, in October, 1,451
Dialogue: 0,0:32:04.30,0:32:06.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Americans died of the flu.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:06.15,0:32:09.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The sick clogged the same evacuation lines the
Dialogue: 0,0:32:09.41,0:32:10.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}wounded needed.
Dialogue: 2,0:32:01.50,0:32:07.25,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 845 0 l 845 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:32:01.50,0:32:07.25,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:32:01.50,0:32:07.25,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:32:01.50,0:32:07.25,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}TRAFFIC ON THE ROADS · MEUSE-ARGONNE
Dialogue: 0,0:32:24.54,0:32:26.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Back home it was the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:26.14,0:32:29.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}At Walter Reed in Washington, the flu caused more
Dialogue: 0,0:32:29.16,0:32:32.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}than 2,000 admissions and more than a hundred and
Dialogue: 0,0:32:32.17,0:32:32.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}fifty deaths.
Dialogue: 2,0:32:24.79,0:32:30.54,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1063 0 l 1063 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:32:24.79,0:32:30.54,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:32:24.79,0:32:30.54,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1919 · FORD FILM COLLECTION, NATIONAL ARCHIVES
Dialogue: 3,0:32:24.79,0:32:30.54,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}U.S. ARMY GENERAL HOSPITAL NO. 36 · DETROIT
Dialogue: 0,0:32:41.70,0:32:43.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And it hit the healers hard.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:43.53,0:32:46.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}More than 21,000 Army nurses served in the war.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:46.59,0:32:49.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}More than 10,000 of them went overseas.
Dialogue: 2,0:32:41.95,0:32:47.70,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1188 0 l 1188 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:32:41.95,0:32:47.70,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:32:41.95,0:32:47.70,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:32:41.95,0:32:47.70,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}FIELD HOSPITAL TENTS AND ARMY NURSES · 28TH DIVISION
Dialogue: 0,0:33:35.89,0:33:37.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}They worked under fire too.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:37.74,0:33:40.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Nurse Beatrice McDonald lost an eye to a shell
Dialogue: 0,0:33:40.90,0:33:44.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}splinter at a British casualty clearing station in
Dialogue: 0,0:33:44.34,0:33:45.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}August 1917.
Dialogue: 2,0:33:36.14,0:33:41.89,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1188 0 l 1188 132 l 0 132{\p0}
