Dialogue: 3,0:36:16.00,0:36:21.75,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}U.S. ARMY PHOTO · MEDICAL DEPT. HISTORY, VOL. II (1927)
Dialogue: 3,0:36:16.00,0:36:21.75,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}HOSPITAL TRAIN AT BASE HOSPITAL NO. 27, ANGERS
Dialogue: 0,0:36:41.01,0:36:43.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Here, for the first time in weeks, there were clean
Dialogue: 0,0:36:43.63,0:36:45.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}sheets, and nurses, and time.
Dialogue: 2,0:36:41.26,0:36:45.53,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1017 0 l 1017 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:36:41.26,0:36:45.53,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:36:41.26,0:36:45.53,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:36:41.26,0:36:45.53,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}A U.S. ARMY HOSPITAL WARD · ST. NAZAIRE AREA
Dialogue: 0,0:36:55.09,0:36:56.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And something else.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:56.26,0:36:58.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Women called reconstruction aides.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:58.34,0:37:01.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}They massaged stiff limbs, taught exercises and
Dialogue: 0,0:37:01.22,0:37:04.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}crafts, and helped men learn to use their hands again.
Dialogue: 2,0:36:55.34,0:37:01.09,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 910 0 l 910 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:36:55.34,0:37:01.09,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:36:55.34,0:37:01.09,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:36:55.34,0:37:01.09,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}RECONSTRUCTION AIDES · ST. NAZAIRE AREA
Dialogue: 0,0:37:04.98,0:37:07.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}They often worked 14-hour days, as civilians.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:07.86,0:37:11.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}They were granted veteran status only about 60 years
Dialogue: 0,0:37:11.19,0:37:11.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}later.
Dialogue: 2,0:37:05.23,0:37:10.98,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 910 0 l 910 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:37:05.23,0:37:10.98,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:37:05.23,0:37:10.98,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:37:05.23,0:37:10.98,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}RECONSTRUCTION AIDES · ST. NAZAIRE AREA
Dialogue: 0,0:37:33.02,0:37:35.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}For those who could not go back to the war, the
Dialogue: 0,0:37:35.67,0:37:36.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}chain ended at sea.
Dialogue: 2,0:37:33.27,0:37:37.14,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1017 0 l 1017 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:37:33.27,0:37:37.14,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:37:33.27,0:37:37.14,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1918 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 3,0:37:33.27,0:37:37.14,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}STRETCHERS CARRIED ABOARD SHIP · ST. NAZAIRE
Dialogue: 0,0:37:37.19,0:37:40.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Stretchers were carried aboard ships at the French
Dialogue: 0,0:37:40.74,0:37:42.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}ports, in the rain.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:42.10,0:37:45.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}One of them was the Navy hospital ship USS Mercy.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:45.58,0:37:48.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Beginning in November 1918, she made four round
Dialogue: 0,0:37:48.93,0:37:52.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}trips, and by March 1919 had brought home nearly
Dialogue: 0,0:37:52.35,0:37:53.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}2,000 casualties.
Dialogue: 2,0:37:37.44,0:37:43.19,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 789 0 l 789 132 l 0 132{\p0}
